            "review_title": "Review at Chao Suon Chu Chen",
            "review_text": "Manuel D\n115 contributions\n0\nService and quality of meat destroyed the experience\nDec 2025 • Couples\nWe were looking for a restaurant that specialised in Chao for quite some time so we were really happy when we found this place online.\n\nWhen we got in noone seemed to work there. There were some guests eating but no waiters or waitresses. So after a while standing at the entrance we took a seat. Some minutes later we walken around looking for someone we have found our later waitress sitting with her back facing the entrance all the way in the back of the restaurant.\n\nLooking online we found a great variety of dishes, so we were pretty puzzled when out waitress gave us a small breakfast menu card without prices. Turns out she thought we were hotel guests from the hotel above the restautant. Although we explained in english and vietnamese that we were normal guests she did not understand us.\n\nFrom the small breakfast menu we chose the braised pork porride with coffee and artichoke tea. The artichoke tea is a hibiskus tea, it seems there was a issue with the translator.\n\nAfter ordering the waitress came back 5 minutes later asking for our order again. It just seemed like it was not her day.\n\nThe porridge as is was was perfect and definetly worth 4-5 Stars. Sadly through the pork rips were that tough that we needed many toothpicks. Either the cooking time was not long enough or the quality of the meat was not good enough.\n\nAfterwards while paying it turned out that again the waitress put us in the system as hotel guests. At that point we felt like being pranked.\n\nAll in all the porridge as it is was really fantastic, sadly the service and the meat destroyed what could have been a perfect experience.\nRead more\nWritten December 1, 2025",
